       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1,700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe order may have a typo or a mix-up between the per-dose and daily amounts. These are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you verified it."
